      "imageReview": "PASS for physical scene, visual-canon flag remains. Exact vertical image and companion601149090 individually opened. Rust-colored velvet worm bends down a tree trunk into a moth, whose wing crosses the head region. Segmented soft feet, bark, moth body and wing are cleanly legible; conspicuous eyeshine belongs to the moth. The feeding contact and enclosing wing support the scene. The mouth contact is partly occluded by the moth, which is the point of the selected frame. Do not substitute a generic velvet-worm portrait.",
      "canon": "Full Hugo arc and strange-canon08 read: established adult Peripatoides novaezealandiae complex near Wellington -41.285/174.758, tactile warm/grouchy voice, not a larva becoming a butterfly. Source independently reports P. novaezealandiae, research grade, three current agreeing IDs, Wellington. Taxonomy and home fit the existing provisional complex without narrowing it. IMPORTANT: this source body appears rust/orange with dark markings; earlier Hugo imagery is predominantly dark blue with orange marks. Do not call this a documented individual color change, invent a juvenile recollection to explain it, alter the avatar or quietly widen species. Root must judge visual continuity separately. If the color difference fails continuity, hold this pairing while preserving the literal prose.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Observed: velvet worm feeding on a moth against bark, wing touching/covering the head area. Fiction: wing settling at a particular moment, pause, enclosure comparison, retreat, free antennae, return and choosing more foot contact. No visual acuity claim, species-level moth identification, prey consciousness, flight by Hugo, body transformation, injury joke or unpictured companion. The predator experiences the shape of a flying animal through feeding; he does not become it.",
      "proseAssessment": "PASS for independent review. Brief sensory interruption changes how he resumes the meal. The physical intimacy with a wing gives his established final-shape identity an unfamiliar experience without another walking lesson, cloth metaphor or repeated pleasure from moss. Ends with a concrete bodily adjustment. No regular/article padding.",
      "biologySources": [
        "https://www.doc.govt.nz/nature/native-animals/invertebrates/peripatus-ngaokeoke/",
        "https://teara.govt.nz/en/peripatus/page-2"
      ],
      "biologyEvidence": "Both New Zealand primary institutional accounts independently opened. DOC documents nocturnal invertebrate predation and sticky-fluid capture. Te Ara ecology explains antenna-based prey recognition and external digestion/feeding. No intricate eyesight, exact leg count, slime chemistry or quantitative performance imported. The exact primary observation supplies moth feeding, while the prose sequence is fiction.",
      "operation": "New Story only if root accepts prose, image and color continuity. Preserve all existing bodies, species scope, home and avatar."
