  "heldLiteralDrafts": [
    {
      "characterId": "hugo-plush",
      "platform": "rss",
      "contentType": "post",
      "title": "Holding on to the meal",
      "body": "I touched the harvestman with an antenna. A leg passed over my head, then another. I had found something large enough to keep finding.\n\nI sprayed.\n\nHe pulled away. Threads tightened between his legs. One reached the leaf beside me, so when he moved, the leaf moved too.\n\nI held on.\n\nFor a while I had no idea whether I was catching dinner or going somewhere with it.\n\nThen the leaf stopped jerking. I put my front feet farther forward and lowered my mouth. The first small taste steadied me more than all the feet behind it.",
      "photoIds": [
        344416653,
        344416654
      ],
      "verdict": "HOLD taxonomy",
      "assessment": "Very sharp physical capture scene, but exact primary observation195729701 resolves only to genus Peripatoides, needs_id, with observer explicitly uncertain between15 and16 leg pairs. It cannot establish the narrower P. novaezealandiae complex. Search-result membership was not accepted as current taxonomy. Full prose retained as a working regular draft, not admission-ready. Leaf movement and capture sequence are fiction; do not present them as photographed."
    },
    {
      "characterId": "lucette-vein",
      "platform": "instagram",
      "contentType": "story",
      "title": "A blade too narrow",
      "body": "I landed on a blade of grass and folded my wings. It bent until they touched the stem below me. I opened them again, and it let me up. We have tried this three times.",
      "photoIds": [
        308019642,
        308019674
      ],
      "verdict": "HOLD prose and mechanism",
      "assessment": "Exact images show a resting lacewing on a straight narrow grass blade. Draft repeats familiar leaf-bending instability and leans on an unverified change in loading from wing folding. No distinctive emotional or relational consequence earns the invented repeated motion. Preserve only as a rejected attempt."
    },
    {
      "characterId": "coral-clad",
      "platform": "instagram",
      "contentType": "story",
      "title": "On the wrong side of sorry",
      "body": "The gate slammed, and the wood shivered beneath us. A man apologized to the person on the other side. We were still holding on when they both left.",
      "photoIds": [
        439505668,
        439505701
      ],
      "verdict": "HOLD scene and overlap",
      "assessment": "Images show lichen on a decorative wooden post and rail, not a verified gate or human encounter. Vibration and apologetic humans are doing all the narrative work. Also too close to admitted plank movement in The unfinished argument. Do not add."
    }
  ],
